vk-gitlab reimplements the GitLab-facing side of GitLab Runner, and `vk node` runs the GitLab
jobs a hub places on it as GitLab Runner runs them. Their protocol behaviour (job request, job
update, incremental trace, retries and backoff, failure-reason mapping, token shortening,
system ID) and job execution follow GitLab Runner v19.5.0, from whose Go sources these are
adapted:

- in vk-gitlab: the API client in src/api/client.rs and its types in src/api/types.rs, the
  job trace reporter in src/trace.rs, the JobResponse types in src/job.rs, the failure-reason
  mapping in src/failure.rs, token shortening in src/secret.rs, the system ID in
  src/system_id.rs, the request loop and health checks in src/poll.rs and the cache key
  sanitizer in src/spec.rs;
  the tests in tests/api_compat.rs, tests/trace_compat.rs, tests/job_fixtures.rs,
  tests/spec_translate.rs and unit tests under src/ port test cases and fixtures from GitLab
  Runner's test suite;
- in vk-driver: the job driver under src/node/jobs (output masking, trace, step scripts,
  variables, build settings, artifact transfers, and their tests);
- in vk-agent: the archive rules in src/archive.rs;
- in vk-hub-proto: the failure-reason mapping in src/job.rs and the log line timestamps in
  src/stamp.rs.

Each names the upstream file and test it comes from.
https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab-runner/-/tree/v19.5.0

